window.QUEST = {"six":["sort","straighten","shine","safety","standardize","sustain"],"colours":{"sort":"#CB4B36","straighten":"#BC4B2A","shine":"#D98A2B","safety":"#DDA63A","standardize":"#6E8B5B","sustain":"#4E7A57"},"purpose":{"sort":"Decide what stays. Nothing else.","straighten":"Give what stayed a home you can reach.","shine":"Clean it, and see what the cleaning tells you.","safety":"Fix what could hurt somebody. The fourth S, not the last.","standardize":"Write down what good looks like, so it is not a memory.","sustain":"Attach the reset to something that already happens."},"symptoms":[{"symptom":"Keys, chargers and sunglasses land beside the tray, not in it","room":"Entryway","zone":"Landing Zone","why":"The tray is not where my hand actually opens on the way in","sixS":"Straighten","action":"Empty the tray and the paper stack onto the surface, then give every sheet a verdict: act, file, or recycle, before anything goes back.","victory":"One tray holds only keys and sunglasses, and no loose paper sits anywhere on the surface.","img":"entryway--landing-zone","url":"/zones/entryway-the-landing-spot"},{"symptom":"The rail is full and there is still no empty hook","room":"Entryway","zone":"Coat and Outerwear Zone","why":"There is a coat for a weather category that already has one","sixS":"Sort","action":"Take down every coat that did not go outside once this cold season, and clear the two hooks nearest the door.","victory":"Two hooks stand empty nearest the door, and every coat still on the rail was worn this season.","img":"entryway--coat-and-outerwear-zone","url":"/zones/entryway-the-coats-and-outerwear"},{"symptom":"The counter is never clear","room":"Kitchen","zone":"Primary Prep Counter","why":"Things get set down here on the way past","sixS":"Straighten","action":"Get one unbroken run of counter back, and prove it can hold.","victory":"Your largest cutting board lies flat with room on both sides, and nothing else is on the run.","img":"kitchen--primary-prep-counter","url":"/zones/kitchen-the-primary-prep-counter"},{"symptom":"The junk drawer takes anything","room":"Kitchen","zone":"Utensil and Utility Drawers","why":"The things in it have no home anywhere else","sixS":"Straighten","action":"One drawer, one job, and it closes with one push.","victory":"You can name each drawer's job, and each one closes with one push.","img":"kitchen--utensil-and-utility-drawers","url":"/zones/kitchen-the-utensil-and-utility-drawers"},{"symptom":"The sink is full again by evening","room":"Kitchen","zone":"Sink and Dishwashing Zone","why":"There is no moment in the day when it gets cleared","sixS":"Sustain","action":"Empty basin, dry basin, two tools standing.","victory":"Dry basin, two tools standing, nothing lying in water.","img":"kitchen--sink-and-dishwashing-zone","url":"/zones/kitchen-the-sink-and-dishwashing-zone"},{"symptom":"The counter is covered again two days after I clear it","room":"Primary Bathroom","zone":"Vanity Counter","why":"The things on it are ones we use every single day","sixS":"Sort","action":"Take everything off the counter, wipe the bare stone and the mirror, then put back only the soap, the toothbrush holder and the four products you touched today.","victory":"Bare stone on both sides of the basin, and one tray you can lift with one hand.","img":"primary-bathroom--vanity-counter","url":"/zones/primary-bathroom-the-vanity-counter"},{"symptom":"I clear the desk and it is covered again by the end of the week","room":"Home Office","zone":"Primary Desk","why":"Paper lands here because there is nowhere else to put it","sixS":"Straighten","action":"Take everything off the desk except the monitor, keyboard and mouse. Put the loose paper into the inbox tray, give every sheet in it a verdict until it is under a dozen, and hook the power strip up off the floor.","victory":"One notebook and one tray under a dozen sheets, and the chair rolls the width of the desk without catching.","img":"home-office--primary-desk","url":"/zones/home-office-the-primary-desk"},{"symptom":"The bench is never clear enough to start a job on","room":"Garage","zone":"Primary Workbench","why":"Finished jobs are pushed aside rather than put away","sixS":"Sustain","action":"Clear the bench top down to the vise and the task light, put the current job in one tray, rack the clamps on the rail, and sweep until you can see concrete under the bench.","victory":"A bare bench, one tray holding one job, and swept concrete visible underneath.","img":"garage--primary-workbench","url":"/zones/garage-the-primary-workbench"},{"symptom":"Washing sits in the drum long enough to smell, and gets rewashed","room":"Laundry Room","zone":"Washer and Dryer","why":"Nothing marks the moment a cycle ends","sixS":"Sustain","action":"Empty both drums, take everything off both lids, clear the lint screen and put it back, prop the washer door ajar, and write this month on a strip of tape on the side of the dryer.","victory":"Both drums empty, both lids bare, the door propped open, and a date on the dryer you can read from the doorway.","img":"laundry-room--washer-and-dryer","url":"/zones/laundry-room-the-washer-and-dryer"},{"symptom":"Someone has to move a pile of folded laundry, a stray magazine, or a third throw blanket before they can sit down on the sofa","room":"Living Room","zone":"Sofa and Seating Zone","why":"The laundry doesn't have anywhere else to land on its way through the house, so the sofa catches it","sixS":"Straighten","action":"Pull everything off the seats and dig the seams out: the laundry that migrated here, the second and third throw blanket, the magazines wedged behind the armrest, the coins and hair ties down the back. Sort into leaves-the-room, goes-in-the-wash, and lives-here.","victory":"Every seat is sittable without moving anything, and the throws are folded in one basket.","img":"living-room--sofa-and-seating-zone","url":"/zones/living-room-the-sofa-and-seating"},{"symptom":"A drawer needs a shove or a press-down to close, and it is the one holding workout tops or t-shirts","room":"Primary Bedroom","zone":"Dresser Drawers","why":"You own more of that category than you actually wear, six workout tops when you wear two","sixS":"Sort","action":"Open the drawer that needs a shove to close and pull one full category's worth of overflow out right now: extra workout tops, a wrong-size stack, or loose mothballs, whichever is worst.","victory":"Every drawer closes without being pressed down, and a hand's width of free space shows in each one.","img":"primary-bedroom--dresser-drawers","url":"/zones/primary-bedroom-the-dresser-drawers"},{"symptom":"Homework, mail, or a craft project has been sitting on the table for days, migrating a few inches each evening but never actually leaving","room":"Dining Room","zone":"Dining Table","why":"That activity doesn't have anywhere else in the house to happen","sixS":"Straighten","action":"Clear the whole table onto the floor in one armful, then sort what came off by owner rather than by type. The homework, the unopened mail, and the half-finished craft project each go back to a person, not back to the table.","victory":"The table holds nothing but its centerpiece, and every activity that was on it has gone home with the person who owns it.","img":"dining-room--dining-table","url":"/zones/dining-room-the-dining-table"},{"symptom":"A bottle of bleach sits on the same shelf as an ammonia-based glass cleaner, both within reach from the hallway floor","room":"Hall Closet","zone":"Cleaning Supply Zone","why":"Nobody sorted this shelf by what's safe to store together, only by what fits","sixS":"Safety","action":"Line every bottle up on the hallway floor. Anything decanted into an unmarked spray bottle gets disposed of according to its own instructions, and the specialty cleaner bought for one stain years ago goes with it. Only identical products get poured together.","victory":"Every bottle on the shelf is in its own original, labeled container, and no two different products have been mixed.","img":"hall-closet--cleaning-supply-zone","url":"/zones/hall-closet-the-cleaning-supply-zone"},{"symptom":"A can with a dented seam or a jar with a popped lid is still sitting on the shelf instead of already in the bin","room":"Pantry","zone":"Canned and Jarred Goods","why":"I wasn't sure whether a small dent or a slightly domed lid really counts as spoiled","sixS":"Standardize","action":"Take every can and jar off the shelf, turn each one to find the date, and put anything dented, rusted, bulging or domed straight into the bin rather than back on the shelf.","victory":"No dented, rusted, domed or bulging can or jar remains on the shelf, and every label faces out.","img":"pantry--canned-and-jarred-goods","url":"/zones/pantry-the-canned-and-jarred-goods"},{"symptom":"A game box has been missing one piece for longer than anyone can remember, and it never got a sticky note or a deadline","room":"Family Room","zone":"Board Game and Puzzle Zone","why":"The missing piece is structural, a board section or a single puzzle piece, and the game is already over even though the box still looks fine on the shelf","sixS":"Sort","action":"Pull every box and check its lid for a name label and a tape strip on the short edge. While each one is open, count the pieces against the box's own list. If something is missing, decide now whether it's substitutable (a token, a die, a bill of play money you can replace) or structural (a rules booklet, a board section, a single puzzle piece). Write the missing item and today's date on a sticky note on any box you are not fixing immediately.","victory":"Every box on the shelf is labeled and stacked no more than five high, and any box missing a piece carries a dated sticky note naming exactly what is gone.","img":"family-room--board-game-and-puzzle-zone","url":"/zones/family-room-the-board-game-and-puzzle-zone"},{"symptom":"A box on this shelf has been sealed since a previous address, and nobody can say what's inside without opening it","room":"Guest Bedroom","zone":"Guest Closet","why":"Opening it feels like it could cost an afternoon, so it keeps getting put off","sixS":"Sort","action":"Take everything out and put it on the bed. This closet is where the house keeps holiday decorations, a wedding dress in a zipped bag, a box of old phones, and paperwork from two addresses ago. Sort by whether a named person will use it in a named situation, and route the rest out.","victory":"At least a forearm's width of clear rod carries six matching empty hangers, and the floor square for a suitcase is clear.","img":"guest-bedroom--guest-closet","url":"/zones/guest-bedroom-the-guest-closet"},{"symptom":"A blind cord or looped drawstring hangs down near the pillow, well within reach of a sleeping child's neck","room":"Kids Bedroom","zone":"Bed and Sleep Zone","why":"A cord or loop hanging at a sleeping child's neck height is a strangling risk that outranks how the window dressing looks","sixS":"Safety","action":"Check every blind or curtain cord near the bed head right now and cleat any hanging loop up out of a sleeping child's reach. Strip the duvet and pillow off, count how many stuffed animals were actually in the bed, and move the rest into the basket at the foot where they're still visible. Square the pillow and pull the duvet flat before you finish.","victory":"No cord or loop hangs within reach of the pillow, the bed carries a squared pillow and a flat duvet with only the animals that fit in two arms on top, and the rest sit visible in the basket at the foot.","img":"kids-bedroom--bed-and-sleep-zone","url":"/zones/kids-bedroom-the-bed-and-sleep-zone"},{"symptom":"There's an outfit in the drawer with the tags still on, in a size your baby has already outgrown","room":"Nursery","zone":"Baby Clothing Zone","why":"It was a gift from someone who mattered, and letting it go feels like a small betrayal","sixS":"Sort","action":"Open every drawer, pull anything smaller than what your baby is wearing today, and put it straight into the outgoing bag on the door hook.","victory":"Every drawer holds one size only, and the outgoing bag on the door has something in it.","img":"nursery--baby-clothing-zone","url":"/zones/nursery-the-baby-clothing-zone"},{"symptom":"The reserve roll is mounted low on the wall, and a seated guest has to stand up to reach it","room":"Guest Bathroom","zone":"Toilet Area","why":"It went into whatever holder was already installed, never tested with someone actually seated","sixS":"Safety","action":"Clear everything from the top of the tank and the floor behind the bowl: the collection of air fresheners, the second brush, the magazines, the box of something nobody has identified in years. One reserve roll stays in the open. Nothing else.","victory":"The tank top and the floor behind the bowl are bare except for one reserve roll standing in the open.","img":"guest-bathroom--toilet-area","url":"/zones/guest-bathroom-the-toilet-area"},{"symptom":"A blade guard does not spring back on its own anymore when you release it","room":"Workshop","zone":"Power Tool Storage","why":"A guard that sticks is the injury this zone is actually waiting on, and that outranks how small a fix it seems","sixS":"Safety","action":"Work the retracting guard on every saw with your thumb to confirm it snaps back on its own, and move any battery still sitting on the charger from a finished job onto its tool's hook.","victory":"Every guard snaps shut on its own, and no charger is running behind a job that already ended.","img":"workshop--power-tool-storage","url":"/zones/workshop-the-power-tool-storage"},{"symptom":"The old vacuum has held its corner for over a year, but the main one has never actually broken down long enough to need it","room":"Mudroom","zone":"Cleaning and Utility Zone","why":"Getting rid of a machine that still works feels wasteful, even though it isn't functioning as an actual backup","sixS":"Sort","action":"Shake the door mats out right now, hang the broom back on its clip with the bristles clear of the floor, and check whether the mop head has actually dried. Pull the decanted, unlabeled bottle out of the caddy and label it, or empty it if you can't tell what it is.","victory":"The broom, mop and dustpan all hang clear of the floor, the mop head is dry, and every bottle in the caddy is labeled.","img":"mudroom--cleaning-and-utility-zone","url":"/zones/mudroom-the-cleaning-and-utility-zone"},{"symptom":"Things ride the stair basket for days without ever landing where they actually belong","room":"Stair Landing","zone":"Landing Surface or Console","why":"Nothing marks the moment to carry it, so it waits for a trip that never comes on its own","sixS":"Sustain","action":"Clear the console top and drawer in one sweep: keep only what truly lives on this floor, drop anything headed to another floor straight into the stair basket, and bag up the loose screws, dead pens and read mail that have drifted in.","victory":"The console top holds only its permanent items and an empty tray, and the stair basket on the floor is empty.","img":"stair-landing--landing-surface-or-console","url":"/zones/stair-landing-the-landing-surface-or-console"},{"symptom":"A saucer under a pot is holding standing water days after the last rain, or the upturned wheelbarrow has a puddle sitting in its well","room":"Patio or Deck","zone":"Garden and Plant Care Zone","why":"Checking every saucer only takes ten seconds, but nothing about filling the watering can actually forces you to look down at them first","sixS":"Sustain","action":"Walk the row of saucers, the wheelbarrow well, and any upturned pot lid tipping out standing water, then pull any pot with no drainage hole or last year's dead root ball out of the nested stack.","victory":"No saucer, wheelbarrow well, or pot lid on the patio holds standing water, and every pot in the nested stack has a clear drain hole and nothing dead in it.","img":"patio-or-deck--garden-and-plant-care-zone","url":"/zones/patio-or-deck-the-garden-and-plant-care-zone"}]};
